module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Topologies.HTopology.GeneratorAlmostBlowUpStackMorExists
public import StacksFrontier.CategoryTheory.Sites.Stack.StackBridge.MorSheafFromIsom

/-!
# Descent of morphisms for the criterion of Stacks 0EX9

Conditions (1), (2) and (3) of Stacks 0EX9 — carried here by
`AlgebraicGeometry.BigHOver.IsZariskiStackInGroupoids`,
`AlgebraicGeometry.BigHOver.IsAffineFlatProperFinitePresentationDescent`,
`AlgebraicGeometry.BigHOver.IsOneGeneratorAlmostBlowUpStack` and
`AlgebraicGeometry.BigHOver.IsTwoGeneratorAlmostBlowUpStack` — imply that morphisms of a fibre of
`p : 𝒳 ⥤ (Sch/S)_h` descend along h coverings: a compatible family of morphisms between the chosen
pullbacks of two objects `x` and `y` of the fibre over `U` along an h covering family of `U` is the
family of base changes of a unique morphism `x ⟶ y`.

That is condition (2) of Stacks 02ZI in its family-indexed form, and
`AlgebraicGeometry.BigHOver.isMorSheaf_of_generatorSquares` turns it into the sieve-indexed form
`CategoryTheory.Functor.IsMorSheaf`, which is condition (2) of Stacks 026F and the shape every
consumer of a morphism-sheaf hypothesis in this development takes.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.BigHOver.sieve_ofArrows_pair_mem_topology`: the centre and the modification of
  an almost blowup square of the site generate a covering sieve of the h topology on its base.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.BigHOver.exists_morAgree_id`: a compatible family of local morphisms is
  agreed with by a morphism over `U` itself.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.BigHOver.existsUnique_fiberHom_of_covering`: **descent of morphisms.** A
  compatible family of morphisms between the chosen pullbacks along an h covering family of `U` is
  the family of base changes of a unique morphism of the fibre over `U`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.BigHOver.isMorSheaf_of_generatorSquares`: the same statement in the
  sieve-indexed form, condition (2) of Stacks 026F.

## Implementation notes

**How the three conditions are consumed.**  The property of an object `Y ⟶ U` of the slice
`(Sch/S)_h / U` that is run through
`AlgebraicGeometry.BigHOver.of_localOnGenerators` — the sufficiency direction of Stacks 0EVI on the
slice — is

> there is a morphism between the chosen pullbacks of `x` and of `y` along `Y ⟶ U` which agrees
> with the given family,

`AlgebraicGeometry.BigHOver.MorAgree`.  It is stable under precomposition by
`AlgebraicGeometry.BigHOver.MorAgree.baseChange`, and subterminal by
`AlgebraicGeometry.BigHOver.MorAgree.eq`, so no choice of witness has to be propagated.  Its
Zariski step is `AlgebraicGeometry.BigHOver.morAgree_zariski`.  For a flat proper surjection `g`
of finite presentation onto an affine object it is
`AlgebraicGeometry.BigHOver.morAgree_of_fullyFaithful_toDescentData` for the one-element family
`{g}`, which is an h covering by itself, Stacks 0ETW, and along which the descent-data functor is
fully faithful by condition (2) in its descent form,
`AlgebraicGeometry.BigHOver.IsAffineFlatProperFinitePresentationDescent`.  Its two remaining steps
are two instantiations of `AlgebraicGeometry.BigHOver.exists_morAgree_square`, which produces the
morphism over the base of a cartesian square along which the comparison functor is an equivalence,
at the two shapes of almost blowup square — these are the squares the two halves of condition (3)
are about.

In each case the morphism so produced restricts to the given ones, and agreement with the family is
h local, `AlgebraicGeometry.BigHOver.morAgree_of_covering`, so it suffices that the two legs of the
square cover the base, which is
`AlgebraicGeometry.BigHOver.sieve_ofArrows_pair_mem_topology`, assembled from the geometry of an
almost blowup square recorded in
`AlgebraicGeometry.isProper_finitePresentation_range_union_center_modification`.

**Extraction at the identity.**  What `of_localOnGenerators` returns is a morphism between the
chosen pullbacks along `𝟙 U`, not a morphism `x ⟶ y`.  Conjugating by
`CategoryTheory.Functor.pullbackFiberIdIso` turns it into one, and its base change along `f i` is
read off by `CategoryTheory.Functor.pullbackFiberHom_pullbackFiberIdIso_inv_eq` and
`AlgebraicGeometry.BigHOver.pullbackFiberHom_pullbackFiberIdIso_hom_eq`: the two contractions those
produce are exactly the two halves of `CategoryTheory.Functor.baseChangeFiberMor`, so the agreement
condition at `ε = 𝟙 (V i)` becomes the required equation after
`CategoryTheory.Functor.baseChangeFiberMor_id`.

**From the family-indexed statement to the sieve-indexed one.**  The passage is the one of
`CategoryTheory.Functor.isMorSheaf_of_isomIsSheaf`, run again here from
`AlgebraicGeometry.BigHOver.existsUnique_fiberHom_of_covering` in place of
`CategoryTheory.Functor.existsUnique_fiberHom_of_isomIsSheaf`: every covering sieve is generated by
the family of all of its arrows, `CategoryTheory.Sieve.ofArrows_category`, on which the descent
statement says that `CategoryTheory.Pseudofunctor.toDescentData` is fully faithful, and Mathlib's
`CategoryTheory.Pseudofunctor.IsPrestack.of_isPrestackFor` with
`CategoryTheory.Functor.isPrestack_pullbackPseudofunctor_iff` passes from there to the sheaf
condition on the localized sites.  That lemma itself cannot be applied: its hypothesis is the
family-indexed condition (2) of Stacks 02ZI in the shape
`CategoryTheory.Functor.IsomIsSheafFor`, which quantifies over given restrictions and given fibre
products of the overlaps, and what is available here is the statement about the chosen pullbacks.

